==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ta̠ˈla̠ɾ]|lang=es}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etyl|la|es}} {{term|talari|tālārī|lang=es}}, singular ablative of {{term|talaris|tālāris|lang=la}}, from {{term|tālus|talus|lang=la}}.

====Adjective====
{{es-adj|mf|pl=talares}}

# covering or reaching the [[heel]] (cloth, garment or accesories)

===Etymology 2===
{{etyl|gem|es}} [[zalon]], to [[steal]], [[snatch]].

====Verb====
{{es-verb|tal|ar}}

# to [[cut]], [[cut down]] (particularly a tree, forest)

=====Conjugation=====
{{es-conj-ar|tal}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|es|tala}}
* [[talador]]
* [[talamontes]]

====See also====
* [[deforestar]]

===Etymology 3===
From {{l|es|tala}}, a tree species, from {{etyl|qu|es}} {{term|tara|lang=qu}}.

====Noun====
{{es-noun|m|p=talares}}

# [[tala]] [[groove]].

